<title>USA: U.S. Senate approves $220 million SPR oil sale.</title>
<headline>U.S. Senate approves $220 million SPR oil sale.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Senate on Monday approved a move to sell $220 million worth of oil from the Strategic Petroleum Reserve to help close the budget gap in a catch-all spending bill for the 1997 fiscal year.</p>
<p>The bill, which the House passed Saturday, now goes to President Clinton, who said he would sign it before the start of the new fiscal year at midnight.</p>
<p>The compromise spending bill, covering several agencies' budgets, called for the sale of oil from the emergency stockpile to raise $220 million by Sept 30, 1997.</p>
<p>An Energy Department spokesman said it was unclear yet when the government would begin the auction, which would be the third budget-balancing oil sale since the beginning of this year.</p>
</text>
